     100x100mm footprint, 30mm walls. sim_sorting_grasp.py's BIN_INNER_HALF_MM=47.5mm
     is this bin's usable inner half-opening (measured off this geometry). -->
<!-- 2026-10-04: opening 80 mm (was 95), 3 mm walls (was 5), outer 86 mm (was 105),
     height unchanged. With 100 mm bins the red bin's wall stood 2 cm inside the blue
     bin and the green bin's wall 15 mm inside the red one (MEASUREMENTS.md section 9);
     no reachable layout of four 100 mm bins exists in this workspace. A 70 mm opening
     was tried first and failed the blue probe: a 50 mm cube carried ~30 deg of yaw
     spans ~68 mm and landed propped on the rim, 28 deg from level. -->
